import{_ as a,o as t,c as r,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BdWD-ld-.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-17 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"44 observations and six analyses on authority provenance, stop settlement, delivery, explainable audit and employee applications.","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-17 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"44 observations and six analyses on authority provenance, stop settlement, delivery, explainable audit and employee applications.","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-17.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-17.md","lastUpdated":1794885097000}'),o={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-17.md"};function i(s,e,l,p,c,d){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="_2026-11-17-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-17 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-17-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-17 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The highest-priority research questions are <strong>preventing agent messages from impersonating human authority; distinguishing returned Stop/timeout from stopped effects; and distinguishing child output from delivery and acceptance by its parent.</strong> Orca, Codex, OpenHands, Paperclip and ADK supply concrete fixes or open counterexamples. The AAE A2A-extension discussion adds request binding and accepted-but-failed versus rejected-and-not-invoked semantics, still an open proposal.</p><p>This run contains <strong>44 observations → six analyses</strong>. Execution started at <strong>2026-11-17 10:48:23 Asia/Shanghai (02:48:23 UTC)</strong>. Fresh main Registry contains 47 researchers. The last successful record is <code>2026-11-16T010724Z</code>; no reports are fabricated for missed dates such as November 15. New observations continue per-source successful baselines, while historical pagination gaps remain pending. Event times below are UTC, with release and merge dates distinguished.</p><p>A merge establishes upstream mainline status, not packaged deployment or default enablement unless a Release or official availability announcement is stated. Test numbers are attributed upstream evidence. <strong>No new local experiments, installations, articles or development-review assignments were completed in this monitoring run.</strong> CodeFlowMu/FCoP relationships remain research judgments and unverified candidates.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><p><span id="o1"></span></p><h3 id="o1-kyvvu-path-policies-at-the-kaptein-research-entry" tabindex="-1">O1 Kyvvu path policies at the Kaptein research entry <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-kyvvu-path-policies-at-the-kaptein-research-entry" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 Kyvvu path policies at the Kaptein research entry&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Committed on November 16 at 13:57 UTC: Claude Code Safety manifest 2.0.0, requiring kyvvu-engine 1.1.0. Critical rules deny, high rules ask the developer, and low rules allow and record. Secret-read history constrains subsequent outbound actions, but only within the last enforcement_history_limit task steps, default 10,000, including model entries. This is not permanent session taint. Shell regex can miss indirection and needs filesystem/network controls. The author is kyvvu-bot, not proof of Kaptein personally committing or an entirely open platform.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/Kyvvu/manifests/commit/d7062e2de2b42144219f387106d81e44b1aa204f" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o2"></span></p><h3 id="o2-orca-separates-agent-mail-from-human-authority" tabindex="-1">O2 Orca separates agent mail from human authority <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-orca-separates-agent-mail-from-human-authority" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 Orca separates agent mail from human authority&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 18:50 UTC, #43093. Agent mail previously entered the recipient as ordinary user text; upstream reports a real Codex run treating it as explicit human authorization for a risky upload. The fix injects a retrieval pointer and delivers the actual message through a tool with provenance, while retaining the sender in the UI. A person in the local Orca window can approve a Codex-denied action once. The reproduction is upstream, not our experiment. Learning value high; governance competitive risk and tracking priority increase, while Orca remains in the second radar circle.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43093" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o3"></span></p><h3 id="o3-orca-repository-hook-trust-extends-to-future-changes" tabindex="-1">O3 Orca repository hook trust extends to future changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-orca-repository-hook-trust-extends-to-future-changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 Orca repository hook trust extends to future changes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 21:50 UTC, #42890. Always trust covers future repository orca.yaml changes, and an existing version approval is treated as repository trust. Run once stays bound to the displayed content hash; automations require persistent trust. VM and certain multi-host repository cases retain version checks. This reduces interruptions while widening supply-chain trust, not universally improving safety. Learning value high; assess this risk separately from O2 and add trust migration to radar tracking.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/42890" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o4"></span></p><h3 id="o4-codex-freezes-review-evidence-and-carries-enclosing-call-context" tabindex="-1">O4 Codex freezes review evidence and carries enclosing call context <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-codex-freezes-review-evidence-and-carries-enclosing-call-context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 Codex freezes review evidence and carries enclosing call context&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17 at 00:59 and 02:32 UTC. #61929 freezes ordered ReviewCutoff views so later evidence, including revocation, does not leak into an earlier review. #61946 matches host-verified enclosing tool names and arguments by call ID while keeping the nested action under review. Ambiguous or missing context is omitted and cannot displace screenshots or ordinary evidence. guardian_nested_approval_context defaults off. Mainline merge does not establish rollout to every client.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61929" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61946" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o5"></span></p><h3 id="o5-codex-isolates-late-turn-completion-from-current-approvals" tabindex="-1">O5 Codex isolates late turn completion from current approvals <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-codex-isolates-late-turn-completion-from-current-approvals" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 Codex isolates late turn completion from current approvals&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 12:14 and 16:38 UTC. #61801 limits cancellation/status effects to the latest started turn, preventing an earlier terminal event from clearing a newer approval. #61841 emits Declined and item/completed when a late background-command approval is canceled, retaining its original turn ID and reaching replacement subscribers. These changes concern approval ownership and terminal receipts, not merely presentation.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61801" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61841" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o6"></span></p><h3 id="o6-codex-distinguishes-acceptance-wakeup-and-interruption" tabindex="-1">O6 Codex distinguishes acceptance, wakeup and interruption <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-codex-distinguishes-acceptance-wakeup-and-interruption" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 Codex distinguishes acceptance, wakeup and interruption&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Three PRs MERGED November 16, 22:07–23:58 UTC. send_message acknowledges acceptance and advises followup_task to activate an idle non-root recipient. The default-off interrupt_at_item_boundary retains the current output item, cancels tools immediately, marks unexecuted calls aborted, and waits for the turn terminal event before follow-up. Interrupting compaction preserves summaries and completed answers. Message acceptance is not execution, and interruption does not erase completed output.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61894" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61909" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61916" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">3</a></p><p><span id="o7"></span></p><h3 id="o7-codex-tool-call-attribution-through-designated-proxies" tabindex="-1">O7 Codex tool-call attribution through designated proxies <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-codex-tool-call-attribution-through-designated-proxies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 Codex tool-call attribution through designated proxies&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 19:14 UTC, #61860. Attribution is opt-in for CODEX_TOOL_CALL_ATTRIBUTION_PROXY and carries the controller tool-call ID on HTTP or outer HTTPS CONNECT. Caller-supplied attribution is stripped; direct destinations and other proxies receive none. This associates network requests with calls, but does not by itself prove an effect or valid authorization.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61860" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o8"></span></p><h3 id="o8-claude-code-2-1-326-fixes-background-identity-and-mcp-isolation" tabindex="-1">O8 Claude Code 2.1.326 fixes background identity and MCP isolation <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-claude-code-2-1-326-fixes-background-identity-and-mcp-isolation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 Claude Code 2.1.326 fixes background identity and MCP isolation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 16 at 22:11 UTC. Notes include stopping before model requests if the background gateway environment is lost; avoiding termination of another user’s reused PID; recording managed PreToolUse denials in telemetry; isolating parallel MCP results saved in the same millisecond; and extending remote Stop to background subagents. These are upstream release statements, not locally reproduced guarantees of complete governance.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.326" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o9"></span></p><h3 id="o9-agents-python-preserves-input-and-handoff-history-after-restore" tabindex="-1">O9 Agents Python preserves input and handoff history after restore <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-agents-python-preserves-input-and-handoff-history-after-restore" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 Agents Python preserves input and handoff history after restore&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 22:53 through November 17 at 01:20 UTC. #6042 prevents duplicate normalized input after staging a message during approval, failing before server acceptance, then saving/restoring and retrying. #6041 recognizes serialized single-text handoff summaries so later handoffs do not nest them repeatedly. These repair history and checkpoint compatibility, not exactly-once external effects.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6042" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6041" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o10"></span></p><h3 id="o10-agents-python-binds-decisions-to-pending-calls-and-retains-checks" tabindex="-1">O10 Agents Python binds decisions to pending calls and retains checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-agents-python-binds-decisions-to-pending-calls-and-retains-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 Agents Python binds decisions to pending calls and retains checks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 22:52–23:00 UTC. The demo REPL previously treated y as a new chat turn, leaving the paused tool unresolved; it now displays the pending action, applies the decision to it and resumes. Output guardrails retain already-completed sibling results once before canceling pending checks, excluding results produced only during cancellation cleanup.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6045" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6040" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o11"></span></p><h3 id="o11-agents-python-counts-usage-from-failed-attempts" tabindex="-1">O11 Agents Python counts usage from failed attempts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-agents-python-counts-usage-from-failed-attempts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 Agents Python counts usage from failed attempts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 23:00 UTC, #6046. HTTP and WebSocket runs record provider-reported usage for failed/incomplete Responses before raising, including response spans. Non-streaming retries count each attempt’s reported usage once whether retry succeeds or exhausts its budget. This improves failure-cost visibility, without establishing exact costs when providers report no usage.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6046" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o12"></span></p><h3 id="o12-agents-js-preserves-edited-mcp-replay-and-surviving-spans" tabindex="-1">O12 Agents JS preserves edited MCP replay and surviving spans <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-agents-js-preserves-edited-mcp-replay-and-surviving-spans" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 Agents JS preserves edited MCP replay and surviving spans&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17 at 01:02 and 01:03 UTC. Hosted MCP replay takes output from the current typed item instead of stale provider metadata, preserving empty strings and honoring edits, redactions and deletion. Console tracing skips an unserializable span, warns with counts, and exports the remaining entries. Mainline fixes do not establish a new npm release.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2672" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2670" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o13"></span></p><h3 id="o13-agents-js-proposes-preserving-terminal-sibling-tool-results" tabindex="-1">O13 Agents JS proposes preserving terminal sibling tool results <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-agents-js-proposes-preserving-terminal-sibling-tool-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 Agents JS proposes preserving terminal sibling tool results&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Created November 17; #2673 remains OPEN, non-draft and unmerged. It proposes evaluating toolUseBehavior against already-completed sibling results in original call order after approval, avoiding an extra model call. Only newly completed tools emit events/write Session, and restored receipts are checked against history. This is a proposal to follow, not shipped behavior.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2673" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o14"></span></p><h3 id="o14-openhands-prevents-synthetic-goals-from-answering-human-questions" tabindex="-1">O14 OpenHands prevents synthetic goals from answering human questions <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-openhands-prevents-synthetic-goals-from-answering-human-questions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 OpenHands prevents synthetic goals from answering human questions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Experimental ask_user and follow-up #6902 MERGED November 16 at 16:06 and 20:23 UTC. Pending questions precede Stop hooks and completion loops. Goal start/resume rejects pending_ask, and generated messages carry sender=goal so they cannot impersonate answers. Option indices disambiguate identical labels. Upstream supplies HTTP/WebSocket and real-model evidence; we have not installed/tested it, and experimental gating remains.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6902" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6852" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o15"></span></p><h3 id="o15-openhands-corrects-messages-through-append-only-events" tabindex="-1">O15 OpenHands corrects messages through append-only events <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-openhands-corrects-messages-through-append-only-events" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 OpenHands corrects messages through append-only events&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 20:46 UTC, #6876; message_edits defaults off. Agents can correct their own prior messages still visible in context by appending MessageEditEvent. Clients render the latest edit while EventLog remains append-only; the model retains its original message and edit tool call/result. Messages condensed out of view cannot be edited. This separates presentation corrections from original evidence.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6876" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o16"></span></p><h3 id="o16-openhands-adds-runtime-mcp-tools-with-a-first-step-barrier" tabindex="-1">O16 OpenHands adds runtime MCP tools with a first-step barrier <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-openhands-adds-runtime-mcp-tools-with-a-first-step-barrier" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 OpenHands adds runtime MCP tools with a first-step barrier&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 15:59 and 19:11 UTC. Runtime add_mcp_servers is add-only, rejecting legacy protocol/SSE, without removal, replacement or global writeback. New tools receive server prefixes without renaming existing tools. Agent Server returns a conversation after a one-second startup budget, but the first model step still waits for servers to join or fail. SDK default behavior still waits for all servers.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6802" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6877" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o17"></span></p><h3 id="o17-openhands-lets-organizations-disable-public-defaults" tabindex="-1">O17 OpenHands lets organizations disable public defaults <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-openhands-lets-organizations-disable-public-defaults" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 OpenHands lets organizations disable public defaults&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 11:47 UTC, #6739. OH_PUBLIC_SKILLS_ENABLED=false disables default public skills; OH_PUBLIC_CATALOG_ENABLED=false disables default public skill/plugin catalog fetching. Registered organization marketplaces, supplied and persisted skills remain. Both default true and conflict precedence is deferred. These are source controls, not a complete enterprise allowlist or skill safety verification.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6739" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o18"></span></p><h3 id="o18-github-mcp-server-2-2-ships-skills-and-controlled-automation-tools" tabindex="-1">O18 GitHub MCP Server 2.2 ships skills and controlled automation tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-github-mcp-server-2-2-ships-skills-and-controlled-automation-tools" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 GitHub MCP Server 2.2 ships skills and controlled automation tools&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 16 at 23:30 UTC. Opt-in skills expose 18 bundled workflows filtered by available tools, not execution authorization. #3719 adds 11 automation read/write/run tools behind a non-default toolset and agent_automations flag. Mutations require exact-request form acceptance expiring after ten minutes and fail closed without state protection; HTTP hides them when protection is missing. hide_secret=true avoids retrieving secret values, but is not the default. Skills/redaction merged earlier; the new event is their release.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/releases/tag/v2.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/3719" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/3685" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">3</a> · <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/3838" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">4</a></p><p><span id="o19"></span></p><h3 id="o19-copilot-enterprise-controls-customization-provenance" tabindex="-1">O19 Copilot enterprise controls customization provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-copilot-enterprise-controls-customization-provenance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 Copilot enterprise controls customization provenance&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Official November 16 announcement: strictPluginOnlyCustomization can restrict standalone user/project skills, agents, hooks, MCP servers and executable extensions, retaining plugins and managed settings. Marketplace restrictions require strictKnownMarketplaces; plugin-only is not itself an allowlist. Availability is scoped to enterprise-issued Business/Enterprise seats on Enterprise Cloud. Announced available, not verified in our tenant.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-16-control-where-github-copilot-customizations-come-from/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o20"></span></p><h3 id="o20-copilot-announces-local-harness-retirement-with-separate-sandbox-controls" tabindex="-1">O20 Copilot announces Local harness retirement with separate sandbox controls <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-copilot-announces-local-harness-retirement-with-separate-sandbox-controls" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 Copilot announces Local harness retirement with separate sandbox controls&quot;">​</a></h3><p>November 16 announcement: VS Code 1.146 deprecates Local harness, with removal planned for February 2027. Copilot harness has defaulted for new sessions since 1.143 and shares runtime with CLI/App. Session continuity depends on a live Agent Host, and editor tools need the editor connected. Selecting the harness does not enable sandboxing or ensure customization compatibility. Retirement is planned, not completed.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-16-vs-code-retires-the-local-harness-in-february-2027/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o21"></span></p><h3 id="o21-copilot-adds-mobile-continuity-in-chat-reauthentication-and-finer-scheduling" tabindex="-1">O21 Copilot adds mobile continuity, in-chat reauthentication and finer scheduling <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-copilot-adds-mobile-continuity-in-chat-reauthentication-and-finer-scheduling" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 Copilot adds mobile continuity, in-chat reauthentication and finer scheduling&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The November 16 official weekly digest lists mobile continuation of Cloud/Codespace sessions, MCP reauthentication within a conversation followed by resume, and minute/custom-cron Project automations. Cross-workspace attention-prioritized Inbox remains experimental. GHES App access is GA, but GHES cloud sessions are unavailable. This is newly checked official weekly evidence, not a claim that every feature merged today. Mobile exception handling has high learning value; product competitive risk increases; continue observing.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-16-github-copilot-weekly-releases-november-9/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o22"></span></p><h3 id="o22-paperclip-confirms-stop-only-after-preparation-settlement" tabindex="-1">O22 Paperclip confirms Stop only after preparation settlement <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-paperclip-confirms-stop-only-after-preparation-settlement" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 Paperclip confirms Stop only after preparation settlement&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 20:38 UTC, #21906. A pre-dispatch stop previously saved no-provider-start proof but left the receipt requested. Under the run lock, settlement checks absence of handedOffAt and other conditions, writes preparation_settled, then confirms Stop. A stale controller with handoff evidence retains its recovery hold. Stop does not restart work; a later message uses normal admission. High learning value and recovery competitive risk; Paperclip remains a main-radar priority.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21906" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o23"></span></p><h3 id="o23-paperclip-preserves-credential-entry-points-across-controller-takeover" tabindex="-1">O23 Paperclip preserves credential entry points across controller takeover <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-paperclip-preserves-credential-entry-points-across-controller-takeover" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 Paperclip preserves credential entry points across controller takeover&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 20:13 UTC, #21928. A surviving provider process kept its old PATH to gh/git launchers; deleting the former controller’s random directory made credentials appear expired. Session/task-stable launcher paths are now re-armed by the adopting controller. This restores continuity, not permanent authority; revocation and credential expiry need separate checks. High learning value; add identity continuity to the radar.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21928" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o24"></span></p><h3 id="o24-paperclip-limits-reserve-overflow-to-the-excess-call" tabindex="-1">O24 Paperclip limits reserve overflow to the excess call <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-paperclip-limits-reserve-overflow-to-the-excess-call" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 Paperclip limits reserve overflow to the excess call&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 18:53 UTC, #21913. With 768 KiB reserved per pending call and an 8 MiB turn budget, transient reservation overflow previously stopped the whole turn and required manual Retry. Now only the excess call receives a retryable rejection; real retained-byte overflow can still stop the turn, with a fresh-session continuation backstop. Thresholds are implementation-specific. Learn the separation of backpressure and durable receipts; recovery competitive risk increases.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21913" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o25"></span></p><h3 id="o25-paperclip-retains-human-and-child-completion-semantics-when-coalescing-wakes" tabindex="-1">O25 Paperclip retains human and child-completion semantics when coalescing wakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-paperclip-retains-human-and-child-completion-semantics-when-coalescing-wakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 Paperclip retains human and child-completion semantics when coalescing wakes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Three PRs MERGED November 16 at 16:10/16:37 through November 17 at 01:59 UTC. Human comments coalesced into system wakes reopen terminal tasks based on actual comment authors. All merged reasons survive so unconsumed child results remain visible to the parent finish gate. A successfully finalized blocker can release dependencies after its later workspace operation settles and its run ends; unsuccessful finalize remains blocking. #21918 explicitly rejects an alleged finish-delay attribution in the test; do not report it as a proven incident. High learning value; retain main-radar priority.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21914" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21918" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21948" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">3</a></p><p><span id="o26"></span></p><h3 id="o26-orkas-releases-recoverable-creative-workflows-with-explicit-acceptance-gaps" tabindex="-1">O26 Orkas releases recoverable creative workflows with explicit acceptance gaps <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-orkas-releases-recoverable-creative-workflows-with-explicit-acceptance-gaps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 Orkas releases recoverable creative workflows with explicit acceptance gaps&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 16 at 15:28 UTC; #223 merged. Changes include Content/commerce workbenches, recoverable video timelines, image/PDF/Office handling and conversation/project/local-task recovery. Upstream retains latency findings of 796.4 ms versus 500 ms and 1377.3 ms versus 1000 ms, initial context above 20K, quit-IPC and document-recovery gaps, without new physical Windows/Linux or signed-binary acceptance. MIT source excludes packaged shared projects, cloud sync and web-app publishing. High learning value and increasing delivery competition; maturity needs independent experience.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/releases/tag/v2026.11.16" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/223" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">3</a></p><p><span id="o27"></span></p><h3 id="o27-paradev-publishes-immutable-agent-tool-drives-per-bundle" tabindex="-1">O27 Paradev publishes immutable agent-tool drives per bundle <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-paradev-publishes-immutable-agent-tool-drives-per-bundle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 Paradev publishes immutable agent-tool drives per bundle&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17 at 01:21 and 02:41 UTC. Per-organization gating enables bundle/region read-only Vercel Drives for agent CLIs. Publishing stops the writer before snapshot mounting, avoiding corruption of a still-written drive. Follow-up publishing forks older drives, fetches changes, writes the manifest last and smoke-checks each agent; failures explicitly report kept-previous or dropped. MIT project, with Vercel cost/dependency for this cloud path. High learning value; operations/distribution competition increases. Preserve original Superset radar attribution and verified canonical ParadevAI/Paradev.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9844" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9861" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o28"></span></p><h3 id="o28-paradev-re-registers-oauth-clients-only-on-specific-invalid-client-evidence" tabindex="-1">O28 Paradev re-registers OAuth clients only on specific invalid-client evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-paradev-re-registers-oauth-clients-only-on-specific-invalid-client-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 Paradev re-registers OAuth clients only on specific invalid-client evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 23:10 UTC, #9848. Before reusing a dynamic OAuth client, an authorization-endpoint probe discards it only on a 4xx explicitly identifying the client as invalid. Network failures, unrelated 403s and 5xx preserve existing registration and grant binding. Each reused connection adds a GET capped at five seconds. Upstream checked requests/tests, not deployed end-to-end acceptance. High learning value for recovery criteria; moderate integration competition; continue observing.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9848" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o29"></span></p><h3 id="o29-paradev-guards-workspace-sleep-by-sandbox-session-generation" tabindex="-1">O29 Paradev guards workspace sleep by sandbox session generation <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-paradev-guards-workspace-sleep-by-sandbox-session-generation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 Paradev guards workspace sleep by sandbox session generation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 04:18 UTC, #9800. Cloud workspaces record sandbox_session_id/expiry, using expiry watches and a 30-minute reconcile for missing platform events. Asleep writes are session-bound so a stale stop cannot overwrite a newly awakened sandbox. Database expand/contract supports old and new status names during rollout. Upstream attributes the race discovery to TLA+; we did not run that verification. High learning value; track generation guards and upgrade compatibility.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9800" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o30"></span></p><h3 id="o30-orca-reads-sessions-without-waking-and-records-actual-launch-settings" tabindex="-1">O30 Orca reads sessions without waking and records actual launch settings <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-orca-reads-sessions-without-waking-and-records-actual-launch-settings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 Orca reads sessions without waking and records actual launch settings&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 22:07 and 23:11 UTC. orca agent list/show/read addresses host sessions and transcripts by Orca session ID without screen scraping or starting/waking agents; cross-host selection and sleeping-terminal/WSL limitations remain. Chat-worker receipts record effective model/effort after placement rather than only requested values; terminal unknowns remain null. High observability learning value, moderate governance competition; increase tracking priority alongside O2.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/41815" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43276" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o31"></span></p><h3 id="o31-crewai-returns-at-timeout-without-claiming-worker-termination" tabindex="-1">O31 CrewAI returns at timeout without claiming worker termination <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-crewai-returns-at-timeout-without-claiming-worker-termination" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 CrewAI returns at timeout without claiming worker termination&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 16:53 UTC, #9324. Synchronous max_execution_time now raises on deadline rather than waiting for ThreadPoolExecutor shutdown, using shutdown(wait=False, cancel_futures=True). Python cannot forcibly stop an already-running thread, so tools may continue in the background. Reassigning work after timeout may overlap the original execution; this is not a complete cancellation-effects solution.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9324" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o32"></span></p><h3 id="o32-crewai-counts-scoped-memory-independently-of-capped-scans" tabindex="-1">O32 CrewAI counts scoped memory independently of capped scans <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-crewai-counts-scoped-memory-independently-of-capped-scans" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 CrewAI counts scoped memory independently of capped scans&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 03:31 UTC, #9391. Scoped LanceDB counts previously derived from scans capped at 50,000 rows; native count_rows now uses the same scope-prefix filter. Categories and oldest/newest metadata still derive from capped scans, so not all statistics become exhaustive. This informs long-running employee observability, not authorization isolation.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9391" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o33"></span></p><h3 id="o33-adk-has-open-fixes-for-delegated-output-and-remote-task-recovery" tabindex="-1">O33 ADK has open fixes for delegated output and remote task recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-adk-has-open-fixes-for-delegated-output-and-remote-task-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 ADK has open fixes for delegated output and remote task recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>#8185 was created November 16 and remains OPEN: child output reaches the event stream but not parent ctx.output, leaving downstream input None; it proposes use_as_output propagation. #7849 is an October-created OPEN fix updated November 16: resuming callers first GetTask for successfully completed task-mode peers rather than messaging a terminal task. Plain chat and failed/canceled peers have different scope. Neither is merged; upstream test claims are not our results.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/pull/8185" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/pull/7849" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o34"></span></p><h3 id="o34-langfuse-aggregates-deletion-audits-while-retaining-object-lookup" tabindex="-1">O34 Langfuse aggregates deletion audits while retaining object lookup <a class="header-anchor" href="#o34-langfuse-aggregates-deletion-audits-while-retaining-object-lookup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O34 Langfuse aggregates deletion audits while retaining object lookup&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 17:26 UTC, #20322. A 1,000-trace deletion becomes one project deleteTraces audit event rather than 1,000 actor lines/rows, retaining the entire traceIds snapshot. Typed resource refs are derived consistently for live and backfill lookup. Lower audit cost depends on a reconstructable object set, not a summary saying bulk completion. Merge time alone does not establish inclusion in release 4.81.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20322" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o35"></span></p><h3 id="o35-langfuse-audit-migration-fixes-its-boundary-and-deduplication-identity" tabindex="-1">O35 Langfuse audit migration fixes its boundary and deduplication identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#o35-langfuse-audit-migration-fixes-its-boundary-and-deduplication-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O35 Langfuse audit migration fixes its boundary and deduplication identity&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 14:15 UTC and listed in the 16:26 UTC v4.81.0 release. Postgres-to-ClickHouse audit backfill checkpoints every 500 rows by (created_at,id), waits five minutes for commits, fixes copyUntil with a ten-minute overlap, and shares event IDs with staging. Existing copies are skipped to preserve actor metadata; unmappable rows count as failedRows. Read-path migration remains separate; copying does not mean every query switched.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/18958" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/releases/tag/v4.81.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o36"></span></p><h3 id="o36-yue-zhao-s-auditable-0-5-makes-audit-stage-and-method-type-explicit" tabindex="-1">O36 Yue Zhao’s auditable 0.5 makes audit stage and method type explicit <a class="header-anchor" href="#o36-yue-zhao-s-auditable-0-5-makes-audit-stage-and-method-type-explicit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O36 Yue Zhao’s auditable 0.5 makes audit stage and method type explicit&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 16 at 01:28 UTC, after the previous run’s start and absent from its report. Rows/boards add Type and Algorithm, with PRE/LIVE/POST when stages mix, explicit Custom/Baseline/Oracle boundaries, and generated README boards checked against golden files. This improves benchmark interpretation and documentation/API table contracts, not a new batch of detectors or higher local scores. Positional table parsers need migration.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/yzhao062/auditable/releases/tag/v0.5.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o37"></span></p><h3 id="o37-phoenix-otel-exposes-ignored-sampling-and-processor-configuration" tabindex="-1">O37 Phoenix OTEL exposes ignored sampling and processor configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o37-phoenix-otel-exposes-ignored-sampling-and-processor-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O37 Phoenix OTEL exposes ignored sampling and processor configuration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17 at 01:58 UTC with corresponding @arizeai/phoenix-otel 3.1.0 release at 02:11 UTC. register warns on ignored OTEL sampler/span environment variables and exposes sampler/spanLimits. Positional processor arguments fail clearly instead of silently dropping spans. Upstream package probes showed ignored always_off could still export data; browser builds were not exercised. Governance must consider both missing audit and unintended export.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/pull/17837" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/%40arizeai/phoenix-otel%403.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o38"></span></p><h3 id="o38-gemini-cli-validates-executable-targets-behind-trusted-mcp-configuration" tabindex="-1">O38 Gemini CLI validates executable targets behind trusted MCP configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o38-gemini-cli-validates-executable-targets-behind-trusted-mcp-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O38 Gemini CLI validates executable targets behind trusted MCP configuration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 17:56 UTC, #30283. Trusted system MCP configuration is insufficient when its script or parent directory is writable by less-privileged users, allowing code substitution under an allowlisted identity. The fix validates local commands/interpreter scripts, warns and skips insecure entries, and blocks lower-priority workspace definitions from shadowing those names. Enterprise trust extends beyond the JSON file.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30283" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o39"></span></p><h3 id="o39-openhands-1-41-requires-an-actual-answer-to-replace-a-secret" tabindex="-1">O39 OpenHands 1.41 requires an actual answer to replace a secret <a class="header-anchor" href="#o39-openhands-1-41-requires-an-actual-answer-to-replace-a-secret" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O39 OpenHands 1.41 requires an actual answer to replace a secret&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 16 at 13:41 UTC and included in the 20:46 UTC 1.41.0 release. request_secret for an existing name previously returned saved without an answer. It now waits for Save/Cancel, only upserts the requested name, never fetches/prefills the old value, and returns not_saved without writing on cancel. Graham Neubig appears explicitly as requester/reviewer. Upstream live Canvas checks are not our local acceptance.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/pull/19062" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/releases/tag/v1.41.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a></p><p><span id="o40"></span></p><h3 id="o40-orca-proposes-cleanup-without-reauthorizing-revoked-paths" tabindex="-1">O40 Orca proposes cleanup without reauthorizing revoked paths <a class="header-anchor" href="#o40-orca-proposes-cleanup-without-reauthorizing-revoked-paths" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O40 Orca proposes cleanup without reauthorizing revoked paths&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Created November 17 at 02:17 UTC; #43371 remains OPEN, non-draft. It proposes closing an existing watcher by its in-memory path key after worktree removal/revocation, without granting new filesystem access or creating watchers. Scope is local POSIX; Windows/SSH behavior is unchanged. High learning value for post-revocation cleanup; competitive maturity remains proposal-level. Continue observing, not a shipped fix.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43371" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o41"></span></p><h3 id="o41-adk-proposes-consistent-oauth-redaction-across-log-sinks" tabindex="-1">O41 ADK proposes consistent OAuth redaction across log sinks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o41-adk-proposes-consistent-oauth-redaction-across-log-sinks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O41 ADK proposes consistent OAuth redaction across log sinks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Created November 17 at 01:22 UTC; #8195 remains OPEN, non-draft. BigQuery analytics misses OAuth code/verifier/response-URI fields already redacted by debug logging; it proposes four-key and URL/text coverage. Reproduction is function-level, not a live OAuth-to-BigQuery leak. private_key_id is an identifier, not a secret. Six focused cases pass but ten full-file failures remain; do not report full validation or a confirmed production leak.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/pull/8195" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o42"></span></p><h3 id="o42-mini-swe-agent-proposes-per-instance-trajectory-saving" tabindex="-1">O42 mini-SWE-agent proposes per-instance trajectory saving <a class="header-anchor" href="#o42-mini-swe-agent-proposes-per-instance-trajectory-saving" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O42 mini-SWE-agent proposes per-instance trajectory saving&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Created November 16 at 21:54 UTC; #1051 remains OPEN, non-draft. Shared agent.output_path makes parallel SWE-bench workers write one file, while defaults save instance trajectories only at completion. It proposes per-instance step saving that preserves completed steps after exceptions. Upstream used deterministic local workers, without provider/container integration. Reruns still use preds.json and do not resume these trajectories. This concerns evaluation evidence isolation, not new checkpoint resume.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/SWE-agent/mini-swe-agent/pull/1051" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o43"></span></p><h3 id="o43-codex-restores-sandbox-ssh-while-retaining-host-key-checks" tabindex="-1">O43 Codex restores sandbox SSH while retaining host-key checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o43-codex-restores-sandbox-ssh-while-retaining-host-key-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O43 Codex restores sandbox SSH while retaining host-key checks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17 at 02:33 UTC, #61947. User namespaces can make root-owned SSH drop-ins appear owned by nobody and OpenSSH rejects them. Filesystem-restricted commands now mask /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d with a read-only empty directory, preserving explicit grants. Masked settings such as KnownHostsCommand do not run, while upstream handshake tests still reject changed host keys. This compatibility fix changes configuration semantics, not removal of SSH authentication.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61947" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a></p><p><span id="o44"></span></p><h3 id="o44-a2a-aae-proposal-separates-authorization-decisions-from-skill-outcomes" tabindex="-1">O44 A2A AAE proposal separates authorization decisions from skill outcomes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o44-a2a-aae-proposal-separates-authorization-decisions-from-skill-outcomes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O44 A2A AAE proposal separates authorization decisions from skill outcomes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>An author update on OPEN Issue #2391, November 16 at 13:17 UTC, describes request_digest binding to frozen requests; paired accepted-but-failed skills versus rejected-and-never-invoked skills; deferred decision/ratification; and implementation provenance statements. hummbl’s clean_room 24/24 is participant-reported and its result PR was pending submission. Sponsorship for an experimental extension repository and maintainer guidance on challenge/refusal mapping remain outstanding. We did not recompute vectors or verify live wire interoperability. This is complementary pre-skill authorization research, not A2A core standard or an automatic FCoP requirement.</p><p>Primary sources：<a href="https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/issues/2391" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/issues/2391#issuecomment-6917526766" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/issues/2391#issuecomment-6917489248" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">3</a></p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-priority-research-message-provenance-must-not-become-execution-authority" tabindex="-1">A1 Priority research: message provenance must not become execution authority <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-priority-research-message-provenance-must-not-become-execution-authority" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 Priority research: message provenance must not become execution authority&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o1">O1</a>、<a href="#o2">O2</a>、<a href="#o3">O3</a>、<a href="#o4">O4</a>、<a href="#o5">O5</a>、<a href="#o10">O10</a>、<a href="#o14">O14</a>、<a href="#o18">O18</a>、<a href="#o19">O19</a>、<a href="#o38">O38</a>、<a href="#o39">O39</a>、<a href="#o44">O44</a>。</p><p>Supported: Orca, OpenHands, Agents SDK and GitHub MCP distinguish agent mail, synthetic goals, human decisions and exact-request acceptance; Codex adds evidence cutoffs. Enterprise governance needs provenance and the specific approved action beyond allow/deny. Persistent repository trust is a different tradeoff. Unverified locally: collapsing employee delegation, comments and human approval into user text in an adapter could lose authority boundaries. P0 experiment candidate: drive one harmless test upload via agent mail, system notice and explicit human approval, then vary expiry, changed parameters and revocation. Assert effects and decision binding, not a reviewer’s safe label. Compare sender/delegation/evidence expression at FCoP; identity, current permissions and enforcement belong to Runtime/adapters. Costs include identity, digest and authorization-version management and possible human delay. Interaction topic: prevent an old quoted human authorization from being reused for a new action.</p><h3 id="a2-priority-research-verify-stop-timeout-takeover-and-settlement-separately" tabindex="-1">A2 Priority research: verify stop, timeout, takeover and settlement separately <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-priority-research-verify-stop-timeout-takeover-and-settlement-separately" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 Priority research: verify stop, timeout, takeover and settlement separately&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o5">O5</a>、<a href="#o6">O6</a>、<a href="#o8">O8</a>、<a href="#o9">O9</a>、<a href="#o13">O13</a>、<a href="#o22">O22</a>、<a href="#o23">O23</a>、<a href="#o24">O24</a>、<a href="#o25">O25</a>、<a href="#o29">O29</a>、<a href="#o31">O31</a>、<a href="#o33">O33</a>、<a href="#o40">O40</a>。</p><p>Supported: timely CrewAI TimeoutError does not kill a running thread; Paperclip distinguishes stop request, handoff, no-start proof and settlement; Paradev generation guards prevent stale stop writes. Caller return and execution termination need separate evidence, without implying every framework has the same fault. P0 experiment candidate: interrupt a uniquely identified countable local action before preparation, after handoff, after effect but before receipt, during controller restart, and with a late old terminal event; also transfer timed-out work to a backup employee. Measure duplicates, orphan processes, unsettled receipts, latency and manual ambiguity. Define thresholds before execution. FCoP can compare task/event/result/evidence contracts; leases, owner generations, retries and process termination belong to Runtime. Costs include fault injection and retained uncertainty. Interaction topic: what evidence permits recovery when a tool received the action but its outcome is unknown?</p><h3 id="a3-audit-must-explain-omissions-corrections-aggregation-and-history-windows" tabindex="-1">A3 Audit must explain omissions, corrections, aggregation and history windows <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-audit-must-explain-omissions-corrections-aggregation-and-history-windows" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 Audit must explain omissions, corrections, aggregation and history windows&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o1">O1</a>、<a href="#o7">O7</a>、<a href="#o11">O11</a>、<a href="#o12">O12</a>、<a href="#o15">O15</a>、<a href="#o32">O32</a>、<a href="#o34">O34</a>、<a href="#o35">O35</a>、<a href="#o36">O36</a>、<a href="#o37">O37</a>、<a href="#o41">O41</a>、<a href="#o42">O42</a>。</p><p>Supported: logging alone is insufficient. OpenHands appends corrections, Langfuse retains object sets/stable IDs when aggregating, Phoenix exposes both missing and unintended telemetry, and Kyvvu states a bounded history window. Unverified locally: final-only employee summaries could hide failed cost, policy-window limits and evidence gaps. P1 experiment candidate: inject a malformed span, redacted correction, secret read crossing the history window, 1,000-object batch, failed-model usage and concurrent trajectory writes. Verify original provenance, explainable edits, complete sets and explicit loss counts. auditable 0.5 is a candidate for stage-aware comparisons, not a combined safety guarantee. FCoP can compare evidence/correction semantics; collection, storage, export access and retention are Runtime/operations. Costs involve privacy, indexing and storage. Interaction topic: prove aggregate object completeness without re-recording sensitive values.</p><h3 id="a4-priority-research-completion-requires-delivered-and-consumed-results" tabindex="-1">A4 Priority research: completion requires delivered and consumed results <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-priority-research-completion-requires-delivered-and-consumed-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 Priority research: completion requires delivered and consumed results&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o6">O6</a>、<a href="#o9">O9</a>、<a href="#o13">O13</a>、<a href="#o14">O14</a>、<a href="#o16">O16</a>、<a href="#o25">O25</a>、<a href="#o30">O30</a>、<a href="#o33">O33</a>、<a href="#o44">O44</a>。</p><p>Supported: ADK child output in an event stream need not reach parent context; coalesced Paperclip wakes must retain child-completion reasons; Codex acceptance is not wakeup. Distinguish acceptance, execution, artifact production, handoff, parent consumption and independent acceptance. P0 experiment candidate: a research→synthesis→independent-review three-role flow with reordered artifacts/messages, duplicates, paused parents and children completed before resume. Verify the right artifact versions reach parent context and incomplete delivery can be rejected by the reviewer. Compare FCoP semantics with A2A task/artifact/authorization outcomes and AAE request_digest; MCP readiness/skill catalogs are complementary integration, not automatically same-layer competitors. AAE cross-run counts remain participant claims requiring independent recomputation and separate wire tests. Costs include version/consumption tracking; no FCoP core change is yet established. Interaction topic: route child artifacts arriving after parent cancellation to history, reopen, or independent acceptance?</p><h3 id="a5-persistent-employees-need-controlled-skill-supply-and-upgradeable-environments" tabindex="-1">A5 Persistent employees need controlled skill supply and upgradeable environments <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-persistent-employees-need-controlled-skill-supply-and-upgradeable-environments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 Persistent employees need controlled skill supply and upgradeable environments&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o3">O3</a>、<a href="#o8">O8</a>、<a href="#o16">O16</a>、<a href="#o17">O17</a>、<a href="#o18">O18</a>、<a href="#o19">O19</a>、<a href="#o20">O20</a>、<a href="#o23">O23</a>、<a href="#o27">O27</a>、<a href="#o28">O28</a>、<a href="#o29">O29</a>、<a href="#o38">O38</a>、<a href="#o43">O43</a>。</p><p>Supported: catalog toggles, organization source restrictions, script permissions, immutable drives, OAuth registration recovery and status compatibility address distinct links. Public defaults remain enabled in OpenHands; Copilot plugin-only still needs marketplace controls; Orca repository trust includes future versions. Record these defaults in trials. Unverified inference: fixed roles/SOPs can still change behavior through CLI, hook and connector upgrades, motivating effective versions/identities. Experience candidates: pinned Paperclip, Orca and Paradev for restart/upgrade/access comparisons. Vercel Drive is not a zero-dependency local delivery solution. FCoP can compare artifact/version declarations; installation, dependencies, sandboxing, credentials and rollback belong to Runtime/product delivery. Costs include compatibility, storage, OS permission differences and failed-update fallback. Interaction topic: make the shift from approved bytes to future repository content visible and revocable.</p><h3 id="a6-competitor-and-application-research-should-prioritize-recovery-and-delivery" tabindex="-1">A6 Competitor and application research should prioritize recovery and delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-competitor-and-application-research-should-prioritize-recovery-and-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 Competitor and application research should prioritize recovery and delivery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Evidence：<a href="#o2">O2</a>、<a href="#o3">O3</a>、<a href="#o21">O21</a>、<a href="#o22">O22</a>、<a href="#o23">O23</a>、<a href="#o24">O24</a>、<a href="#o25">O25</a>、<a href="#o26">O26</a>、<a href="#o27">O27</a>、<a href="#o28">O28</a>、<a href="#o29">O29</a>、<a href="#o30">O30</a>、<a href="#o40">O40</a>。</p><p>Supported: Paperclip improves task/wake/stop settlement; Orca provenance and cross-surface observability; Orkas content/business deliverables; Paradev cloud distribution/lifecycle. Their task-company, employee workbench, content-delivery and coding-environment scopes differ; a few PRs do not prove enterprise maturity. Experience order: Paperclip (MIT) for a multi-role parent task, stop/resume and independent acceptance; Orca (MIT) for agent mail, real human approval, mobile takeover and repository trust; Orkas (MIT source separated from packaged commercial features) for an editable document/media deliverable across restart. Paradev (MIT) is a distribution/upgrade reference and later trial candidate. Installation, provider/service credentials and operating costs apply; none were installed or paid-tested this round. Keep all four at high tracking priority, with differentiated recovery, authority/mobile, business-delivery and cloud-efficiency risks. Do not edit Registry or radar circles.</p><h2 id="cross-project-patterns-and-disposition" tabindex="-1">Cross-project patterns and disposition <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-patterns-and-disposition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project patterns and disposition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Authority provenance, stop settlement, result consumption and explainable audit recur in specific changes across this run. That supports studying these mechanisms, not universal convergence, a proven FCoP defect or local effectiveness. Prioritize experiment candidates A1/A2/A4, followed by A3; retain A5 as mechanism references and A6 as experience ordering. None were executed or converted into development tasks. Only technical interaction topics are published; no external comments were sent.</p><h2 id="dual-source-checks-deduplication-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Dual-source checks, deduplication and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#dual-source-checks-deduplication-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dual-source checks, deduplication and limits&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>GitHub</strong>: Fresh Registry’s 47 people and github-engineering entries plus required technology/competitor scopes form 88 original repository entries. Each received commit, Issue/PR collection and Release queries, with URLs, SHAs, states and outcomes saved; selected PRs received detail reads. Additional pages catch up old baselines. Unfinished full pages stay partial and do not advance complete baselines. README/install/license depth focused on selected applications; Discussions/Roadmaps and all older issue comments were not exhausted. Two GitHub links are one source type.</li><li><strong>Access and historical gaps</strong>: TSA-AI-Workforce still returns 404 for all three APIs, not proof of shutdown or no change. Original superset-sh/superset redirects; GitHub and the official site establish ParadevAI/Paradev, whose recent commits were checked. The original historical gap remains. Paperclip/Orca historical commits and some Issue/Release pagination are unfinished. Partial, inaccessible and unexamined material are recorded separately, never as exhaustive no-change coverage.</li><li><strong>Non-GitHub</strong>: Opened Cursor changelog, GitHub changelog and three November 16 announcements, MCP official blog, personal/institutional pages for Yue Zhao, Kaptein, Agrawal, de Witt, Shaokun Zhang and Haoyu Wang, and Paperclip/Orkas/Paradev official sites. Cursor’s current page is headed November 6 and MCP’s November 11; neither is today’s new event. Undated homepage content is not manufactured into news. Haoyu’s linked October/March papers remain older leads. A continuous sweep of all 47 people’s X posts/replies and every company account was not completed; do not interpret this as no social developments.</li><li><strong>People and relationships</strong>: Chinese uses 赵越. Kaptein relates to the Kyvvu policy ecosystem, not an entirely open platform; de Witt’s steganography code is not the official implementation of a multi-agent security survey; Mansura’s bulbasaur-skill-cli is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact. Direct author involvement is recorded only from evidence, such as Graham Neubig in O39; bot commits do not prove personal participation.</li><li><strong>Publication and boundaries</strong>: Only today’s two Markdown reports and two index entries are updated. Existing homepage entry/layout, public snapshots and other content are preserved. Source readback, build, gh-pages publication, exact-commit Pages status and bilingual home→index→full-report checks have separate local receipts; this text does not pre-claim deployment success. No changes to <code>research/runtime/**</code>, business Scheduler/Production/Publication, article candidates or scorecards.</li></ul><p><a href="./">Back to daily intelligence</a> · <a href="./../../../zh/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-17">中文</a></p>',205)])])}const m=a(o,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
